      "expected": "For the LTC4412 ideal-diode circuit, the P-MOSFET source should connect to the output (+5V) and the drain to the input (VBUS_5V_IN) to provide reverse-current protection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "USB page: Q1 pin 2 to VBUS_5V_IN, pin 3 to +5V; U6 LTC4412 SENSE pin 6 to +5V, VIN pin 1 to VBUS_5V_IN."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Reverse-current protection is defeated; the body diode conducts from output to input, allowing backfeed and potential damage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["U12", "R17", "R16"],
      "pins": ["U12.4", "R17.1", "R16.1"],
      "nets": ["+12V", "FB"],
      "observed": "U12 is LM2586S-12 (fixed 12V boost converter) but FB pin 4 is connected to a voltage divider R17=22K, R16=2K instead of directly to +12V.",
      "expected": "For the fixed 12V version, the FB pin should connect directly to the +12V output; if an adjustable version were used, the divider should set 12V (e.g., R17=22K, R16=2.49K).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Power page: U12 LM2586S-12, FB pin 4 connected to R17 22K and R16 2K; output labeled +12V."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Output voltage will be incorrect (approximately 14.8V) or regulation will fail, potentially damaging 12V loads.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_rating",
      "components": ["D3", "U3"],
      "pins": ["D3.1", "D3.2", "U3.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "D3 is MBR0530 (0.5A, 30V Schottky) used as the catch diode for U3 LM2576HVS-5 (3A buck converter).",
      "expected": "The catch diode should be rated for at least the switch current (3A), e.g., MBR340 or SS34.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Power page: U3 LM2576HVS-5, D3 MBR0530 connected between U3 pin 2 (OUT) and GND."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D3 may overheat and fail under load, causing loss of the 5V rail and potential damage.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies detected: Q1 source/drain swapped in the LTC4412 ideal-diode circuit, U12 fixed 12V regulator has an incorrect feedback divider, and D3 catch diode is underrated for the 3A buck converter."
}

